 "Grain by grain, hole by hole. In the old tales the hasty farmer scatters and loses; the counting one gathers the fours and prospers.": "7acf211cfd8c.opus",
 "A hole ripens to four sheaves and is carried to your granary. Patience, in the harvest fables, is always rewarded in fours.": "e3592ffdd7a5.opus",
 "Four gathered. The wise farmer sows the big handful where it will ripen the most holes, not merely the nearest.": "2f6a9fb14fc0.opus",
 "Into the granary. The tale repeats: count, wait, and the harvest falls to the patient.": "1bf8f03d9824.opus",
 "The fields are bare and your granary is fullest. The fable ends as it always does — the careful counter prospers.": "70811059d4f6.opus",
